solution_md:
If  $\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{3}+\sqrt{1990}\in\mathbb{Q}$ , then  $\left(\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{3}+\sqrt{1990}\right)^2\in\mathbb{Q}$ . Write  $$ \left(\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{3}+\sqrt{1990}\right)^2=1995+2\left(\sqrt{6}+\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}\right) $$  It follows that  $\sqrt{6}+\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}\in\mathbb{Q}$  and thus  $\left(\sqrt{6}+\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}\right)^2\in\mathbb{Q}$ . Write
\begin{align*}
\left(\sqrt{6}+\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}\right)^2
&=6+5\cdot 1990+2\left(2\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}+3\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+1990\sqrt{6}\right)
\end{align*}
It follows that  $2\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}+3\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+1990\sqrt{6}\in\mathbb{Q}$  and thus
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+1988\sqrt{6}&=2\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}+3\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+1990\sqrt{6}
&-2\left(\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}+\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+\sqrt{6}\right)\in\mathbb{Q}
\end{align*}
and thus  $\left(\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+1988\sqrt{6}\right)^2\in\mathbb{Q}$ . Write  $$ \left(\sqrt{2\cdot 1990}+1988\sqrt{6}\right)^2=2\cdot 1990+6\cdot 1988^2+2\cdot 1988\cdot 2\sqrt{3\cdot 1990} $$  It follows that  $\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}\in\mathbb{Q}$  and denote  $\sqrt{3\cdot 1990}=\frac{p}{q}$ , where  $p,q\in\mathbb{Z}$  and  $q\ne 0$  and w.l.o.g.  $\gcd(p,q)=1$ . Then  $$ p^2=3\cdot 1990\cdot q^2 $$  That is,  $p^2$  is even, and we must  $p$  be even (for if  $p$  is odd, then  $p^2$  is odd). Denote  $p=2k$  for some  $k\in\mathbb{Z}$ , then  $$ 3\cdot 1990\cdot q^2=p^2=4k^2\quad\Longrightarrow\quad 3\cdot 995\cdot q^2=2k^2 $$  which also implies  $q$  is even. Hence we get  $\gcd(p,q)\neq 1$  that contradicts to the assumption.

