We consider complex numbers with  $\odot ABC$  as the unit circle. The problem condition requires us to prove that  $$ -\frac{b-c}{b-e} \cdot \frac{(c-b)^2}{(c-e)^2} \in \mathbb{R} \iff \frac{(b-c)^3}{(b-e)^2(e-c)} \in \mathbb{R}. $$    $$ \color{blue} \clubsuit\color{blue} \boxed{\textbf{Calculations.}}\color{blue} \clubsuit $$  Notice that, due to the problem condition, we have  $a=a, b=a^3$  and,  $\textbf{WLOG}$ ,  $c=1$ . (this is well-known and need not to be proven)
Since  $CD=2 \cdot BD$ , we have   $$ d=\frac{1}{3} \cdot (2 \cdot a^3+1) $$   and   $$ e=2d-a=\frac{1}{3}\cdot(4a^3-3a+2); $$  all that remains is to prove is that
\[
\frac{(b-c)^{3}}{(e-b)^{2}(e-c)}
   =\frac{(b-1)^{3}}
          {\biggl(\dfrac{4b+2c-3(a+b)}{3}\biggr)^{2}
           \biggl(\dfrac{4b+2c-3a-3}{3}\biggr)}
   =\frac{27(b-1)^{3}}
          {(b-3a+2)^{2}(4b-3a-1)}
\]
\[
=\frac{27(a^{3}-1)^{3}}
       {(a^{3}-3a+2)^{2}(4a^{3}-3a-1)}
