\end{align*}

Now, by AM-GM,  $x+y+z \geq 3$  and  $x^2+y^2+z^2\geq xy+yz+zx$    
So,  $3(x^2+y^2+z^2) \geq x^2+y^2+z^2+ 2(xy+yz+zx) = (x+y+z)^2 \geq 3(x+y+z)$     $\implies x^2+y^2+z^2 \geq x+y+z$  $\implies (x^2+y^2+z^2)(x+y+z) \geq (x+y+z)^2 \geq 3(x+y+z)$     $\implies\displaystyle \sum_{cyc}x^3 +\sum_{cyc} xy^2+\sum_{cyc} x^2y \geq 3(x+y+z)$  $\implies\displaystyle 3\sum_{cyc}x^3 \geq \sum_{cyc}x^3 +\sum_{cyc} xy^2+\sum_{cyc} x^2y \geq 3(x+y+z)$  [By Muirhead's inequality]    $\implies x^3+y^3+z^3 \geq x+y+z\ .....(i)$  

Again,  $x^2+y^2+z^2 \geq x+y+z$     $\implies x^2y^2+y^2z^2+z^2x^2 \geq xy+yz+zx$  [As,  $xy\times yz\times zx =1$ ]     $\implies x^4+y^4+z^4\geq x^2y^2+y^2z^2+z^2x^2 \geq xy+yz+zx$  [By Muirhead's inequality]    $\implies x^4+y^4+z^4 \geq xy+yz+zx\ .....(ii)$ Again by AM-GM,  $x^4+y^4+z^4\geq 3\ .....(iii) $     
