Suppose, FTSOC, that for sufficiently large  $n$ , we have \[1+ a_n \le a_{n-1}\sqrt[n]{2}.\] Then we have 
    \begin{align*} 1+a_n &= 1+ \frac{a_n\sqrt[n+1]{2}}{\sqrt[n+1]{2}}
    &\ge 1+ \frac{1+a_{n+1}}{\sqrt[n+1]{2}}
    &= \boxed{1+ \frac{1}{\sqrt[n+1]{2}}+ \frac{a_{n+1}}{\sqrt[n+1]{2}}}
    &= 1+ \frac{1}{\sqrt[n+1]{2}}+ \frac{a_{n+1}\sqrt[n+2]{2}}{\sqrt[n+1]{2} \cdot \sqrt[n+2]{2}}
    &\ge 1+ \frac{1}{\sqrt[n+1]{2}}+ \frac{1+a_{n+1}}{\sqrt[n+1]{2} \cdot \sqrt[n+2]{2}}
    &= \boxed{1+  \frac{1}{\sqrt[n+1]{2}}+ \frac{1}{\sqrt[n+1]{2} \cdot \sqrt[n+2]{2}}+ \frac{a_{n+2}}{\sqrt[n+1]{2} \cdot \sqrt[n+2]{2}}}.
    \end{align*}
    We can repeat this process to get 
    \begin{align*}a_n &\ge \left(\sum_{k=1}^m \frac{1}{\prod_{i=1}^k \sqrt[n+i] {2}}\right) + 
    \left(\frac{a_{n+m}}{\prod_{j=1}^m \sqrt[n+j] {2}}\right)
    &\ge \sum_{k=1}^m \frac{1}{\prod_{i=1}^k \sqrt[n+i] {2}}.
    \end{align*}
    But \[\sum_{k=1}^m \frac{1}{\prod_{i=1}^k \sqrt[n+i] {2}} = \Theta\left(m^{1- \log{2}}\right) \to \infty.\]
    So  $a_n$  is arbitrarily large, and we have a contradiction.

