         &\cos \theta_1 \cos \alpha_1 \sin \alpha_1 + \cos \theta_1 \cos \alpha_1 \cos \alpha_2 \sin \alpha_2 + \cdots + \cos \theta_1\cdots \cos \alpha_{k - 1} \sin \alpha_{k - 1} 
         &< \sqrt{k - 1} \cos \theta_1.
    \end{align*}
    Adding  $\cos \theta_1 \sin \theta_1 = \frac{1}{2} \sin(2\theta_1)$  to both sides, this is equivalent to \begin{align*}
        &\cos \theta_1 \sin \theta_1 + \cos \theta_1 \cos \alpha_1 \sin \alpha_1 + \cdots + \cos \theta_1 \cos \alpha_1 \cdots \cos \alpha_{k - 1} \sin \alpha_{k - 1} 
