    \end{align*}
    We want to show that the LHS in the above inequality is less than  $\sqrt{k}$  to complete the inductive step. Thus, to show that, it suffices to prove that for all integers  $k \ge 2$ , \[\sqrt{k - 1} \cos \theta + \frac{1}{2} \sin (2\theta) \le \sqrt{k}.\]
    We will prove a restated statement: for all positive real numbers  $a$  and any  $\theta \in [-\pi, \pi]$ , \[(a + \sin \theta) \cos \theta \le \sqrt{a^2 + 1}.\]
