Otherwise  $\triangle PCE$  lies strictly inside  $\triangle PAF$ , hence  $[PBD]<[PAF]$ , contradiction.  $\blacksquare$ Now let  $A=(1:0:0)$ ,  $B=(0:1:0)$  and  $C=(0:0:1)$ . Let  $P=(x:y:z)$ , where  $x+y+z=1$ , we have   $$ D=(0:y:z),\hspace{5pt}E=(x:0:z)\text{ and } F=(x:y:0) $$  Then from the above assumptions,  $x>1>z>0>y$ Therefore,
\begin{align*}
