 x(i+iMk)+yk+z & = & 0 
 (k^2-iMk)y \quad  - kz & = & 0 
\end{array}


\end{cases} \]

From linear algebra we know in order to get a non-trivial solution (in fact infinitely many of them) for the system of equations above, we must have \[ \begin{vmatrix}
i+iMk  \quad & k & 1 
