Thus,  $\triangle AGH \sim \triangle AFE$ .

Thus, if  $EFGH$  is a rectangle, then  $CB = GH = FE$ . Therefore,  $\triangle AGH \cong \triangle AFE$ . So,  $AC = AF$ . Therefore,  $\triangle AFC$  is equilateral, and  $\angle AFC = 60^{\circ}$ . Thus,  $\angle ADC = 30^{\circ}$ . Thus,
\begin{align*}
\angle ADC &= 30^{\circ} 
\angle DAB + \angle DBA &= 30^{\circ} 
\left(90 - \angle ACB\right) + \angle ABC &= 30^{\circ} 
\angle ACB - \angle ABC &= 60^{\circ}.
\end{align*}

If  ${\angle ACB - \angle ABC = 60^{\circ}}$ , then reversing the above steps, then  $\triangle AFC$  is equilateral. Hence,  $\triangle ABC \cong \triangle AGH \cong \triangle AFE$ .

Let  $P$  and  $Q$  be the foot of the perpendiculars from  $A$  to  $FE$  and  $GH$ , respectively. Then, 
\begin{align*}
