I will prove just the normal version. The generalization is basically the same proof.**Notation:** for any discrete random variable  $X$ , denote its entropy by   $$ H(X) := -\sum_{s} \mathbb P(X=s)\log\mathbb P(X=s). $$  The answer is  $\boxed{3/32}$ , achieved by taking an arbitrarily large clique. To prove the bound, take a uniform (ordered)  $K_4$  subgraph  $WXYZ$  of  $G$ . Then, using [Shearer's Lemma](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shearer%27s_inequality), we get
\begin{align*}
3\log(24g(G)) &= 3H(W,X,Y,Z) 
&\leq H(W,X,Y) + H(X,Y,Z) + H(Y,Z,X) + H(Z,X,W) & \text{(Shearer)}
&= 4H(X,Y,Z) 
&\leq 4\log(6f(G)), &\text{(uniform bound)}
\end{align*}
giving  $(24g(G))^3 \leq (6f(G))^4$ , proving the bound for  $c=6^4/24^3 = 3/32$ .

