Now apply 2 points DDIT on the incircle and  $X$  and  $Y$  as the tangency points. This gives that  $(AX,AY)$ ,  $(AB,AC)$  and  $(AT,AT)$  swap under some Involution. Projecting this Involution onto  $BC$  from  $A$ , we get that  $(P,Q)$ ,  $(B,C)$  and  $(\infty_{BC},\infty_{BC})$  swap under some Involution.

Now finally note that the Involution on  $BC$  by a reflection across  $M$  is an Involution that swaps  $(B,C)$  and  $(\infty{BC},\infty_{BC})$ . So this must be the Involution that we found out earlier and so  $MP=MQ$  and we are done.

