Let  $UVW$  be the orthic triangle of  $ABC$ , and let  $Q=(AH)\cap(ABC)$ . We'll first show that  $M,H,Q$  collinear.

Let  $\phi_H$  be inversion at  $H$  with power  $HA\cdot HU$ . We see that  $\phi_H((AH))=BC$  and  $\phi_H(ABC)=(UVW)$ , so  $\phi_H(Q)=(UVW)\cap(BC)=M$ . Therefore,  $Q,H,M$  are collinear.

We'll now show that  $AQDE$  is cyclic. Note that
\[\angle WHD=\pi/2-\angle WDH=\pi/2-\angle VEH=\angle VHE,\]
so  $DE$  bisects  $\angle(WC,VB)$ . Thus, by the angle bisector theorem,  $WD/DB=WH/HB=VH/HC=VE/EC$ . Let  $\sigma$  be the spiral similarity that sends  $WB$  to  $VC$ . By the ratio equality we just proved, we see that  $\sigma(D)=E$ . Note that the center of this spiral similarity is  $(AWV)\cap(ABC)=Q$ , but since it sends  $DB$  to  $EC$ , it's also  $(ADE)\cap(ABC)$ . Thus,  $Q\in(ADE)$ , as desired.

We now see that the radical axis of  $(ADE)$  and  $(ABC)$  is  $AQ$ , and  $AQ\perp QH=HM$ , as desired.  $\blacksquare$

