Let  $F$  be the point on  $(ABC)$  such that  $\measuredangle HFA=90^\circ$  and let  $P$  and  $Q$  be the feet of the altitudes from  $B,C$  in  $\triangle ABC$ . Since  $AH$  is the diameter of  $(APQ)$ ,  $F$  lies on  $(APQ)$ ; therefore  $\triangle FBQ\sim\triangle FCE\iff \measuredangle DBF=\measuredangle QBF=\measuredangle PCF=\measuredangle ECF$ . Since  $\triangle HBD\sim\triangle HCE$  and  $\triangle HBQ\sim \triangle HCP$ , we have \[\frac{BF}{CF}=\frac{BQ}{CP}=\frac{BH}{CH}=\frac{BD}{CE},\] so  $\triangle BDF\sim\triangle BCE$ , so  $F$  is the center of the spiral similarity that takes  $BD$  to  $CE$ , and  $F$  lies on  $(ADE)$ . Since  $M,H,F$  are collinear we are done.

