Clearly  $IA=IK_1=IL_1$ . This means  $\angle AIK_1 = 180^{\circ}-\angle A$ . Thus  $$ \angle K_1IJ = 360^{\circ}-\angle AIK_1-\angle AIC = 360^{\circ}-(180^{\circ}-\angle A) - \left(90^{\circ}+\frac{\angle{B}}{2}\right) = 90^{\circ}+\angle A-\frac{\angle B}{2} $$  and  $$ \angle K_1BJ = \angle ABC - \frac{\angle DBC}{2} = \angle B - \frac{\angle B-(180^{\circ}-2\angle A)}{2} = \frac{\angle B}{2}-\angle A + 90^{\circ} $$  thus  $B, K_1, I, J$  are concyclic. This means  $$ \angle IK_1J = \angle IBJ = \frac{\angle ABD}{2} = 90^{\circ}-\angle A = \angle IK_1L_1 $$  or  $K_1, L_1, J$  are colinear as desired.

