Let  $T = \overline{AD} \cap \overline{BC}$ , and  $S$  be the point on segment  $\overline{TL}$  with  $\angle DSC = \angle APB$ . By the length condition,  $T$ ,  $L$ ,  $K$  are collinear. Observe that  $T$  is the center of homothety that sends  $DSC$  to  $APB$ , and  $DQCS$  is cyclic as   $$ \angle CQD = \angle CBA = 180^\circ - \angle BCD = 180^\circ - \angle BPA = 180^\circ - \angle CSD. $$   Furthermore, since   $$ \angle DQC = \angle CBA = \angle DCT, $$    $(DSCQ)$  is tangent to  $\overline{BT}$  at  $C$ . It follows that   $$ \angle CBP = \angle TCS = \angle TQC = 180^\circ - \angle CQP, $$   implying the result.  $\blacksquare$

