Notice  $E=\overline{AD}\cap\overline{BC}\cap\overline{KL}$  exists and let  $R=\overline{AP}\cap\overline{DQ}$  and  $S=\overline{BP}\cap\overline{CQ}.$  We see  $\triangle ARD$  and  $\triangle BSC$  are perspective from a line, so by Desargues,  $P_{\infty}=\overline{AB}\cap\overline{CD}$  lies on  $\overline{RS}$  and  $\overline{RS}\parallel\overline{AB}\parallel\overline{CD}.$  Noting  $PRQS$  is cyclic, we know \begin{align*}\measuredangle PQC&=\measuredangle PRS=\measuredangle PAB=\measuredangle APB+\measuredangle PBA&=\measuredangle DCB+\measuredangle PBA=\measuredangle ABC+\measuredangle PBA=\measuredangle PBC\end{align*} so  $BCPQ$  is cyclic.  $\square$

