\end{align*}
which is congruent to  $2^{k-1}$  modulo  $2^k$ , as desired.

First, note that for all positive integers  $n$ , we have\[v_2\left[\binom{2^{n+1}}{2^n}\right] = v_2[2^{n+1}!] - 2v_2[2^n!] = (2^{n + 1} - 1) - 2(2^n - 1) = 1\]for all positive integers  $n$  by Legendre. So it remains to show that\[v_2\left[\frac{\binom{2^{n+1}}{2^n}}{\binom{2^{n}}{2^{n-1}}} - 1\right] = v_2[N] - v_2\left[\binom{2^{n}}{2^{n-1}}\right] = 3n-1.\]Using the property that  $2k! = k! \times 2^k \times (2k-1)!!$  for all positive integers  $k$  where we let  $m = 2^{n-1}$ , we may rewrite\begin{align*}
    \frac{\binom{2^{n+1}}{2^n}}{\binom{2^{n}}{2^{n-1}}} - 1&= \frac{(4m)!}{(2m)!^2} \times \frac{m!^2}{(2m)!} - 1&= \frac{(2m)! \times 2^{2m} \times (4m - 1)!!}{(2m)!^2} \times \frac{m!^2}{m! \times 2^m \times (2m - 1)!!} - 1&= \frac{2^m \times m!}{(2m)!} \times \frac{(4m-1)!!}{(2m-1)!!} - 1&= \frac{(4m - 1)!!}{(2m - 1)!!^2} - 1&= \frac{(2^{n + 1} - 1)\ldots (2^n + 1)}{(2^n - 1)!!} - 1&= \frac{(2^{n + 1} - 1)\ldots (2^n + 1) - (2^n - 1)!!}{(2^n - 1)!!}
