To see this, set  $|S| = m$  to be that set for one such interval  $I_1$ . Let  $0 \leq r_i \leq a_1 - 1$  for  $1 \leq i \leq m$  be the remainders when  $(i+1)a_1$  is divided by each of the elements of  $S$ . We may sort  $r_1 \leq r_2 \leq \cdots \leq r_m$ , and the desired sum   $$ \mathcal S(I_1) = r_1^2 + (r_2-r_2)^2 + \cdots + (r_m - r_{m-1})^2 + (a_1 - r_m)^2. $$   For simplification, let  $d_1 = r_1$ ,  $d_i = a_i - a_{i-1}$  for  $2 \leq i \leq m$ , and  $d_{m+1} = a_1 - r_m$ . Now we compute across all  $I_1$  with  $\mathcal F(I_1) = m$ , noting that these  $\mathcal S(I_1)$ 's cover all possible valid combinations of the  $a_i$ :
