Since the circumcircle of  $BIC$  is tangent to  $EF$  (by Fact 5), we have by Power of a Point,  $$ TX \cdot TL = TB \cdot TC = TI^2 = TD \cdot TU, $$  so  $XDUL$  is cyclic, where  $U$  is the foot of the bisector of  $\angle BAC$ . But  $AUML$  is cyclic since  $\angle LAU = \angle LMU = 90^\circ$ . Thus, if  $Y$  is the intersection of  $AM$  and  $XD$ , we have  $$ \angle LAY = \angle LUM = \angle LXD = \angle LXY, $$  so  $LAXY$  is cyclic, implying  $AM$  and  $XD$  meet on  $\Gamma$ , as desired.</details>

