draw((0.7,0.3)--(0,0)--(-0.5,0.5),green);
draw((-0.1,0.9)--(0,0),red);
dot((0,0));
draw((-0.1,0.9)--(0,1)--(0.7,0.3),blue);
draw((0,0)--(-1,0)--(-0.5,0.5),blue);
[/asy]

Note that the linear combinations of  $<1,1>$  and  $<-1,0>$  when starting from the left vertex will span the square, so we are done.

