By Pascal's Theorem on the hexagon  $SSDTTB$ , we get that  $SS\cap TT$  lies on  $AC$ . Now let  $W=SS\cap TT$ . Also let  $WY_1\cap (SDBT)=V'$ .
Since  $\measuredangle WCY_1=\measuredangle ACY_1=\measuredangle ABY_1=\measuredangle TBY_1=\measuredangle WTY_1$ , we get  $WTCY_1$  is cyclic.
This implies that  $\measuredangle DVY_1=\measuredangle DTY_1=\measuredangle CWY'$ , or that  $DV\parallel AC$ .
Now  $-1=(Y_1,V;S,T)\stackrel{D}{=}(DY'\cap AC,P_\infty;A,C)$ , implying that  $DY_1\cap AC$  is the midpoint of  $AC$ .

Similarly,  $ADCX$  is cyclic.
