<blockquote>Let  $P$  be a point on the circumcircle of acute triangle  $ABC$ . Let  $P_A,P_B,P_C$  be the reflections of  $P$  in the  $A$ -midline,  $B$ -midline, and  $C$ -midline. Let  $M_A$  be the midpoint of  $BC$ ,  $M_B$  the midpoint of  $AC$  and  $M_C$  the midpoint of  $AB$ . Let  $H_A$  be the foot from  $A$  to  $BC$ ,  $H_B$  be the foot from  $B$  to  $AC$ ,  $H_C$  be the foot from  $C$  to  $AB$ . 

Let  $O_A$  be the center of  $(PP_AA)$ ,  $O_B$  be the center of  $(PP_BB)$ ,  $O_C$  be the center of  $(PP_CC)$ .

Let  $X$  be the intersection of perpendicular bisector of  $P_AA$  and  $P_BB$ ,  $Y$  the intersection of perpendicular bisector of  $P_BB$  and  $P_CC$  and  $Z$  the intersection of perpendicular bisector of  $P_CC$  and  $P_AA$ .

Show that  $(PP_AA), (PP_BB), (PP_CC),$  and  $(XYZ)$  share a common point.</blockquote>

