Badly written.  $4^{a_j}$  has some excess over  $3^{a_j}$ ; this allows some space for the AM-GM with a large enough constant term (created by a sum of  $2^{a_i}>1$ ) to dominate  $2025\times 3^{a_j}$  instead:
\begin{align*}
\left(\sum_{i=1}^n2^{a_i}\right)^2&>2\left(\sum_{i=1}^{m}2^{a_i}\right)\left(\sum_{j=m+1}^n2^{a_j}\right)+\sum_{j=m+1}^n2^{2a_j}
&>\sum_{j=m+1}^n\left(2m\cdot 2^{a_j}+4^{a_j}\right)
&=\sum_{j=m+1}^n\left(2^{a_j}+\left((2m-1)2^{a_j}+\frac124^{a_j}+\frac124^{a_j}\right)\right)
&\geq\sum_{j=m+1}^n\left(1+3\sqrt[3]{(2m-1)2^{a_j}\times\frac124^{a_j}\times\frac124^{a_j}}\right)
&\geq n-m+\sum_{j=m+1}^n\left(\sqrt[3]{\frac{2m-1}4}\times32^{a_j/3}\right)
&>2025\sum_{i=1}^m3^{a_i}+\sum_{j=m+1}^n\left(2025\times 3^{a_j}\right)
&=2025\sum_{i=1}^n3^{a_i}
\end{align*}
where  $m=\frac{4\times 2025^3+2}{2}$  and  $n>m+\sum_{i=1}^m3^{a_i}$ .

