This is equivalent to proving  $K\in \odot(M,D)$  as we already have  $\angle P^*KM=90^{\circ}$ .
Now  $DL^*\parallel BA$  because  $\angle L^*DH=\angle HFL^*=\angle FEH=\angle DAB$ .

Since line through  $M$  and midpoint of  $BH$  is perpendicular bisector of  $FB$  we also have  $ML^*=MD=MK$  and similarly we also have  $MT^*=MD=MK$  so  $K\in \odot(DL^*KT^*)$ . :yoda:

