We start off with some definitions. Let a  $n-$ *ladder*be a polymino with  $n$  sides consisting of  $\frac{n}{4}$  dominoes, stacked next to each other, in the style of a staircase. Let a  $n-$ *M tile*be a polymino consisting of a  $(n-2)-$ ladder with a single monomino attached to the right of the top-most domino of the ladder. Further, a  $n-$ ladder or M-tile is called*vertical*, if the dominoes which make up the polymino are oriented vertically. Else, we say that it is *horizontal*. For example, a  $12-$ ladder and a  $14-$ M tile, both of which are vertical, are given below.
[asy]
