We want to prove  $BCLK$  is cyclic. 
It's well-known that  $BP=CP$  since  $AP$  is the  $A$ -bisector. Then, realize that  $\measuredangle{PKL} = \measuredangle{PKD} = \measuredangle{PAD} = \measuredangle{EAP} = \measuredangle{ELP} = \measuredangle{KLP}$  implying that  $PK = PL$ . Since  $BC \parallel DE$ , it is trivial to prove that  $\angle{CPL} = \angle{BPK}$  by drawing the perpendicular bisector of  $BC$ . This directly imply that  $\Delta CPL \cong \Delta BPK$ , hence  $BK=CL$ . Therefore,  $BCLK$  is an isosceles trapezoid which finishes the problem.  $\square$ <details><summary>Remark</summary>It is also possible to finish it by proving  $P = BL \cap KC$ .</details>

