We have that  $[\bigtriangleup BCX]=\frac{1}{4}[\bigtriangleup ABC]$ , so  $|AX|=3|BX|$  and  $X=(1/4,3/4,0)$ . Clearly  $Y$  must be the centroid of  $\bigtriangleup ACX$ . Let the intersection of  $CY$  and  $AB$  meet at  $P$ . Then  $|AP|=|PX|$  and  $|AP|=\frac{3}{8}|AB|$ , so  $Y=((5/8)(2/3),(3/8)(2/3),1/3)=(5/12,1/4,1/3)$ . There are 6 pairs of points in this case.

