When  $n$  is odd we have:
\begin{align*}
&2+3+\dots+[ \frac{n-1}{2}-1]+[\frac{n-1}{2}+1]+...+(n-2)+n
&=\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-\frac{(n-1)}{2}-(n-1)-1
&=\frac{n^2+n-n+1-2n+2-2}{2}
&=1.(n-1).\frac{n-1}{2}
\end{align*}
When  $n$  is even we have,
\begin{align*}
&2+3+4+\dots +\dots+[\frac{n}{2}-2]+[\frac{n}{2}]+\dots+(n-1)
&=\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-1-[\frac{n}{2}-1]-n
&=\frac{n^2+n-2-n+2-2n}{2}
&=\frac{n(n-2)}{2}
&=1.\frac{n-2}{2}.n
&=1.[\frac{n}{2}-1].n
\end{align*}

